{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120739","id":3957121887,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7r3ONf","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120739","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120739.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120739.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120739","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120739/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120739/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120739/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a2c001efe15d2b280f84887be04040c60a3f1c47","number":120739,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix Skeleton2D crash and physics multi-thread deadlock","user":{"login":"gebojiang","id":250485739,"node_id":"U_kgDODu4b6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250485739?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang","html_url":"https://github.com/gebojiang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gebojiang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #120552\r\n\r\n### Problem 1: Critical Crash (Segmentation Fault)\r\nWhen a `Skeleton2D` node is freed or during scene reloading, `SkeletonModificationStack2D` can retain a dangling pointer to the deleted skeleton. Accessing this unvalidated pointer during subsequent frames or physics updates leads to random memory corruption and immediate segmentation faults.\r\n\r\n### Problem 2: Multi-threaded Physics Deadlock & Mutex Starvation\r\nTo fix the crash, simply nullifying or cleaning up the pointer synchronously inside the destruction/notification phase introduced an even worse issue when multi-threaded physics was enabled. \r\n1. If the pointer was modified synchronously, it risked racing with the physics thread or mutating state while tree/physics locks were held.\r\n2. If left unhandled, the physics thread would constantly hit `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG` at a very high frequency (e.g., 60Hz to 480Hz+). This slammed the global log/print mutex, causing massive thread starvation that completely froze the main thread, resulting in an unrecoverable deadlock.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nThis PR solves both issues elegantly by decoupling the cleanup phase:\r\n\r\n**Deferred Pointer Nullification (The Core Fix):**\r\nInside the `Skeleton2D` cleanup logic, instead of synchronously forcing `modification_stack->set_skeleton(nullptr)`, we now use `callable_mp` to defer this execution:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (modification_stack.is_valid()) {\r\n    callable_mp(modification_stack.ptr(), &SkeletonModificationStack2D::set_skeleton).call_deferred((Object*)nullptr);\r\n}","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","description":"","color":"885544","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archi